<title>UK: EU Greek, Irish green rates to devalue Friday-HGCA.</title>
<headline>EU Greek, Irish green rates to devalue Friday-HGCA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rates of the Irish pound and the Greek drachma will be devalued with effect from Friday, the UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The green Irish pound will be devalued to 0.757666 per Ecu, compared with the current rate of 0.756658, and the green Greek drachma will be devalued to 311.858 per Ecu compared with 311.761.</p>
<p>Also on Friday, green sterling will enter the fourth of five possible confirmation periods ahead of a revaluation on June 5, the HGCA said.</p>
<p>Green rates are used by the European Union to convert Ecus into the currencies of its member states in its Common Agricultural Policy.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
